# Agent pipeline instructions for __PROJECT_NAME__

Read `CLAUDE.md` first when it exists. It is this project's primary guidance
file; these instructions add lead integration without duplicating or
overriding the project's own constraints.

This repository uses a planner -> implement -> review -> test pipeline.
In Codex, for a feature or bug-fix request, invoke the `feature` skill and act
as its lead. For an agent-toolkit scaffold update, invoke the `toolkit-update`
skill. Do not run either workflow from memory: load the skill and follow its
referenced canonical flow. In OpenCode, use `/feature` or `/toolkit-update`, which select the
`leader` adapter under `.opencode/agents/` and reference the same canonical
Claude instruction files. Do not use the Codex-specific planner adaptation
in an OpenCode-led run. No Claude or Codex CLI is needed for that run.

The task state file under `.agents/` is the only handoff surface between roles.
Keep role replies short and leave full details in that file.

